# Force LF in the working tree on every OS.
#
# This is not cosmetic: EAS Update's runtime fingerprint hashes some tracked
# text files byte-for-byte (`eas.json`, `.gitignore`). EAS builds on Linux (LF),
# so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (CRLF) computes a DIFFERENT
# fingerprint — and `eas update` then publishes under a runtime no installed
# build asks for, so the update silently never arrives. See gotchas.md #53.
* text=auto eol=lf
